Z||000000||SibERThuG||10-14-2000||01:21 AM||||Sometimes, I have a loss of power in my get-up and go. It still moves, but not nearly as quick as other times. Why?? Do I have a loose valve or blown cylinder?? How can I fix this???<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||13
Z||000001||2xsess||10-14-2000||02:18 AM||||I'm not a pro but, it could be a blocked up cat. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-14-2000||02:14 PM||||Could also be a carbonized intake. Get a can of Carb cleaner or Intake cleaner and spray it in there. I noticed a little better performance after doing this.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-14-2000||07:23 PM||||could also be an intermitant vaccum leak, bad ACT sensor(In air cleaner), bad MAP or the vacuum line to it has a problem. TPS making crappy contact internally could also be an issue.<P>whacked out sensors don't always set codes. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||10-15-2000||03:19 AM||||Yeah a wacked vacuum leak or clogged cat b0th will cause that. I was having problems with mine. its just seemed to run out of breath past 3500 rpms. I had to replace the Cat and did have a Vacuum leak. <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A> <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/582bead0.gif"> ||||reg||1
